  "notes": "USAGE:\nぐらぐら is a mimetic word (onomatopoeia) that can function as an adverb, as a noun, or with する. It vividly describes shaking/wobbling or vigorous boiling.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ぐらぐらする: to be wobbly\n- ぐらぐら{揺|ゆ}れる: to shake/rock\n- ぐらぐら{沸|わ}く: to boil vigorously\n- {歯|は}がぐらぐら: a loose tooth\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nがたがた describes rattling or clattering (more noise-focused). ゆらゆら describes gentle swaying (softer, more rhythmic).",
